        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(local-review): use selected Codex CLI",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nUse the operator-selected Codex CLI for local-only reviews and the matching local preflight.\n\n## Problem\n\n`review --local-only` injected `CLAWSWEEPER_PREFER_WINDOWS_CODEX_APP=1`, forcing the Windows Desktop app binary at `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\OpenAI\\Codex\\bin\\codex.exe`. On the reported host that binary is stale and rejects the requested model, while the user's normal `PATH` Codex CLI works. The local preflight selected the same Desktop binary, which could validate a different executable than the review runner.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Stop injecting the Desktop-app preference for local-only reviews.\n- Make `pnpm run codex:local:check` use the same normal `CODEX_BIN`/PATH resolution.\n- Preserve explicit `CODEX_BIN` precedence.\n- Document PATH-based local-only selection and add Windows-oriented launcher regression coverage.\n\nProduction `.github/actions/setup-codex` remains separate and pinned at `@openai/codex` `0.139.0`; this PR does not modify it.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node --test test/codex-process.test.ts test/command.test.ts test/clawsweeper.test.ts` — passed (88 tests).\n- `pnpm run lint:scripts` — passed.\n- `pnpm run build:all` — passed.\n- Focused `oxfmt --check` for changed source, script, and test files — passed.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n- `pnpm run check` ran build and lint successfully, then hit unrelated native-Windows prerequisite failures in existing unit tests: WSL `/bin/bash` unavailable for Bash-helper tests, Windows symlink permission failures, and `npm.cmd` `EINVAL` in runtime packaging. This PR does not broaden into test-harness or platform-policy changes.\n\nProof boundary: native Windows local launcher selection only; no workflow or CI-matrix changes.\n\n## Codex review closeout\n\n- `codex review --uncommitted`: initially found that the preflight still selected a different executable; accepted and fixed that P1.\n- Final `codex review --uncommitted`: clean, with no accepted/actionable findings.\n- `codex review --base origin/main`: clean, with no accepted/actionable findings.\n\n## Risks and rollout\n\nLocal-only review and preflight now use the first spawnable `codex` command on `PATH` unless the operator sets `CODEX_BIN` explicitly. No local CLI is pinned or updated. Production setup remains unchanged. This branch is independent of #539.\n\n",
        "branch": "codex/csw-038-local-only-codex-path",
